🤖 The final test that failed shows the problem that the add method mutates the original Item qty passed in, which is against the requirement in its docstring.

Currently we do:
```python
self.items[item.name].qty += item.qty
```
which changes the existing Item in the store, and in the first insert we set the item directly:
```python
self.items[item.name] = item
```
which means the original item passed is stored and later mutated by += in subsequent adds.

The fix is to always create a new Item instance when adding or merging, so that the original item passed in is never modified.

I will fix the add method accordingly and rerun tests.
